    "text": "Tensor and Contraction"
  },
  {
    "id": "u0002",
    "kind": "prose",
    "token": 4,
    "text": "A tensor maps each named index in its shape to a value.\nA shape is an unordered set of named axes, so `{ N = 4, C = 3 }` and `{ C = 3, N = 4 }` identify the same tensor.\nAn ordered representation of that shape behaves like a familiar multidimensional array.\nA tensor index supplies one value for every axis, so `{ N = 4, C = 3 }` includes indices such as `{ N: 0, C: 0 }` and `{ N: 0, C: 1 }`."
  },
